This file predates the 2026 revival and was never updated to record that
**DONE** here meant "written," not "reachable" -- gmannoise.cpp and
gmanslapi.cpp were exercised by no renderer until Phase 3 gave C++ shaders
a real GMANSurfaceEnv to call them from. Lines below now say **REACHABLE**
where a shader can call the function through env.<name>(...), and
**ORPHANED** where the code this file already marked DONE still has no
caller -- either because Phase 3 did not wrap that particular overload, or
because gmanslapi.h declared a name (distance/ptlined/rotate) gmanslapi.cpp
never defined, a real bug phase-3-REPORT.md records. See AGENTS.md's
"Shading" section for the full GMANSurfaceEnv contract.

