Du, Dv, Deriv			(vector) (vector) (vector;float)
float  random			()
color  random			()
point  random			()
flt|clr|pnt|vect  noise	        (float) (float u,v) (point) (point,float) 		**DONE** gmannoise **REACHABLE** env.noise(...), the four float-returning forms -- **ORPHANED** the color/point/vector out-param overloads
flt|clr|pnt|vect  pnoise        (flt,flt) (flt,flt,flt,flt) (pnt,pnt) (pnt,flt,pnt,flt) **DONE** gmannoise **REACHABLE** env.pnoise(v,pv) and env.pnoise(p,pp) -- **ORPHANED** the (u,v,pu,pv), (p,t,pp,pt) and out-param forms
flt|clr|pnt|vect  cellnoise     (float) (float,float) (point) (point,float) 		**DONE** gmannoise **REACHABLE** env.cellnoise(v) and env.cellnoise(p) -- **ORPHANED** the (u,v), (p,t) and out-param forms

Geometric Functions:
--------------------

xcomp, ycomp, zcomp		(ptype)			**DONE** gmanvector
setxcomp, setycomp, setzcomp	(ptype,float)		**DONE** gmanvector
length				(vector)		**DONE** gmanvector
normalize			(vector)		**DONE** gmanvector
distance			(point p1,p2)		**DONE** gmanslapi **ORPHANED** -- gmanslapi.h declared this lowercase; gmanslapi.cpp only ever defined GMANDistance. No definition of `distance` exists anywhere in the tree; calling it would fail to link. Not fixed -- outside Phase 3's shading path. See phase-3-REPORT.md.
ptlined				(point q,p1,p2)		**DONE** gmanslapi **ORPHANED** -- same gap, GMANPTLined is what is actually defined.
rotate				(point q,a,p1,p2)	**DONE** gmanslapi **ORPHANED** -- same gap, GMANRotate is what is actually defined.
area				(point)
faceforward			(vector n,i,[nref])	**DONE** gmanslapi **REACHABLE** env.faceforward(n,i,nr) -- gmanslapi.h had this exact same lowercase/GMANFaceForward mismatch; fixed as part of wiring it here, see phase-3-REPORT.md.
reflect				(vector i,n)		**DONE** gmanslapi **REACHABLE** env.reflect(i,n), same fix as faceforward above.
refract				(vector i,n;float)	**DONE** gmanslapi **REACHABLE** env.refract(i,n,eta), same fix.
fresnel				(vector i,n;float e,kr,kt;[vector r,t]) **DONE** gmanslapi **REACHABLE** env.fresnel(i,n,eta,kr,kt), same fix (the 7-arg r,t overload is not wrapped -- still **ORPHANED**).
transform			(string;point) (string from,to;point) (matrix;point) (string;matrix;point)
vtranstorm			(string;vector) (string from,to;vector) (matrix;vector) (string;matrix;vector)
ntransform			(string;normal) (string from,to;normal) (matrix;normal) (string;matrix;normal)
depth				(point)
calculatenormal			(point)

